  },
  "summary": "Expose one immutable-context KCS composer without granting history writing authority.",
  "why": "Luis approved Core ownership of reusable production mechanisms, with Semantic Re-entry providing requirements, experiments and the consumer. The history factory reads once; the public pure composer receives immutable coordinates and retained bytes only. The existing history composer delegates to the same serializer and KCS parser. Admission still rejects intervening evidence-only appends. RED 23 expected failures; GREEN history/context 114 passed; full compiler and Shop 755 passed; status and GraphRecipe 52 passed. Exact five-plan Shop evidence remains unchanged. Context consistency is not authentication or sandboxing; source-value agreement, local correction policy, no-op and Re-entry synthesis stay outside Core. No new persisted grammar, fixture semantics, package policy, paper mutation or release claim.",
